The corrected tie-expression exposed a genuine Haskell-backend limitation (`FLOAT.eq` is unavailable), and LLVM also showed that modulo-based tie detection is fragile in this reference model. I’m not adding an unproved equality bridge. Instead, I’m reformulating the implementation around floor/ceiling distances and the semantics’ supported opaque `<` primitive; this is mathematically exact for every finite parsed float and remains symbolically executable without extending the fixed theory.
